ufsbe is a userspace UFS1/UFS2 filesystem driver implemented on top of
FUSE3.  It supports:

  * UFS1 and UFS2 on-disk formats as produced by newfs(8)
  * Soft Updates (softdep)
  * Soft Update Journaling (SUJ) — circular write-ahead log with CRC32
    and automatic replay on unclean unmount
  * LRU buffer cache with write-back and B_BARRIER ordering
  * B-epsilon tree block map — replaces traditional direct/indirect
    block pointers with a write-optimised tree that dramatically
    improves random-I/O throughput (>5x in benchmarks)
  * B-epsilon tree directory index — O(log N) name lookup using a
    64-bit FNV1a hash key; the on-disk linear struct direct layout is
    kept for compatibility with fsck(8) and kernel UFS

The filesystem passes a 30-minute fio endurance suite (14 TiB of I/O,
zero data errors) and is tested on FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.
